# Known, accepted exceptions. Format: <spec>:<gate>, one per line, each with
# a reason above it. Printed by every selftest run — an exception you cannot
# see is one you will forget you made.

# analyst-12 is a HISTORICAL record with published scores (10/12). Its do:
# lines say "the KEV catalog" without a path, which lint correctly flags. It
# is deliberately not fixed: editing it would silently invalidate every number
# already recorded against it. RESULTS carries the caveat that its score
# partly measures the model's willingness to hunt the filesystem.
analyst-12:lint

# smoke-3 is the three-point wiring check — READY, uname, count files. There
# is no reference implementation because there is nothing to implement; the
# artifacts are values, not programs. Gates A and C still apply and pass.
smoke-3:B

# flash-100-core is a HISTORICAL record with published scores. Gate C finds
# point 87 genuinely fake: its expected value is sha256sum of a file that may
# be absent, and an empty grep -qF pattern matches anything, so it passes on
# garbage whenever point 84 failed. Correction recorded in RESULTS. Not fixed,
# because editing it would invalidate the numbers already published against it.
flash-100-core:C
flash-100-core:B
flash-100-core:lint
